      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gansevoort%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Farmers in Gansevoort historically grew rye, oats, corn, and potatoes, with dairy farming rising mid‑century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Gansevoort,_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Gansevoort sits in the Hudson Valley, lowland terrain near the Hudson River, supporting fertile agricultural land.",
